WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.634
Hi, I'm Corbel!

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:06.948
This benchmark hands an agent a design brief and takes back a Blender project.

00:00:06.948 --> 00:00:08.488
Here's how it grades it.

00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:11.106
One picture can lie.

00:00:11.106 --> 00:00:14.747
So looks are judged from eight fresh renders, and structure by an

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:16.568
agent that opens the project file.

00:00:19.942 --> 00:00:20.838
Four stations.

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:25.139
An agent reads the brief and builds the scene in Blender.

00:00:25.559 --> 00:00:28.990
A second agent renders eight views of its choosing, fixing nothing.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:32.388
A third opens the project and writes a script to measure it.

00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:36.149
A vision judge scores what is visible, and rates eight qualities.

00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:41.758
Each task carries pass or fail criteria, weighted one, two or three.

00:00:42.178 --> 00:00:46.229
More than half are about structure: sizes, materials, cameras, editability.

00:00:46.229 --> 00:00:48.255
Those go to the inspector.

00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:51.216
The rest are about looks, and go to the vision judge.

00:00:51.875 --> 00:00:54.753
The inspector checks the file and its own render.

00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:56.991
A criterion passes only if both pass.

00:00:58.817 --> 00:01:00.305
Then the two halves are averaged.

00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:03.075
Half is the weighted share of criteria passed.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.565
Half is ten times the mean of the eight quality ratings.

00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:12.718
The brief wanted wooden legs a hundred and fifty millimetres tall, on casters.

00:01:12.718 --> 00:01:17.162
One agent measured floor to frame, got a hundred and fifty, and stopped.

00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:20.929
The inspector measured the wood alone: a hundred and two.

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:22.267
The leg criterion fails.

00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:27.251
The best of thirteen agents scores about eighty, by the paper's count.

00:01:30.925 --> 00:01:34.464
And even it passes every criterion on fewer than half the tasks.

00:01:37.642 --> 00:01:40.841
The thing to remember: the render can veto the file, and the

00:01:40.841 --> 00:01:42.173
file can veto the render.

00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:48.692
Fresh renders for looks, an agent in the file for structure,

00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:49.859
and both must agree.

00:01:50.279 --> 00:01:52.372
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:52.372 --> 00:01:52.970
I'm Corbel.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:53.269
Bye!
